# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the nxvc test suite.
#
# Everything in here must be a leak we do NOT own and cannot fix. A suppression
# for our own allocation is a bug being hidden; delete it and fix the leak.
# Each entry says which module leaks, why, and how it was observed.
#
# Format: one `leak:<substring>` per line, matched against any function or
# module name in the allocation stack.

# Vulkan ICDs allocate per-process state in a pthread_once initialiser and
# never free it -- the driver's lifetime is the process's, so from its point of
# view there is nothing to free. Observed as a 256-byte direct leak from
# warp.gpu_diff on RADV (AMD RX 7900 XTX, Mesa 1.4.354), where the ICD is
# dlopen'd and its frames do not even resolve to a module name. The only
# resolvable frame in that stack is pthread_once, which is why the suppression
# is written against it.
#
# This is narrow in practice: our own code has no pthread_once one-time
# initialiser that allocates. If that changes, tighten this to the driver
# module name -- and note the name only resolves on some loaders, which is the
# whole reason it is not written that way already.
leak:pthread_once

# The loader itself, when it resolves to a name.
leak:libvulkan.so
leak:libVkLayer
leak:radeonsi_dri.so
leak:libvulkan_lvp.so
leak:libvulkan_radeon.so
